{"chapter": "categories", "node_kind": "definition", "parent_tag": "001R", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$x, y\\in \\Ob(\\mathcal{C})$", "MATH_0002": "$x$", "MATH_0003": "$y$", "MATH_0004": "$x \\times y \\in \\Ob(\\mathcal{C})$", "MATH_0005": "$p\\in \\Mor_{\\mathcal C}(x \\times y, x)$", "MATH_0006": "$q\\in\\Mor_{\\mathcal C}(x \\times y, y)$", "MATH_0007": "$w\\in \\Ob(\\mathcal{C})$", "MATH_0008": "$\\alpha \\in \\Mor_{\\mathcal C}(w, x)$", "MATH_0009": "$\\beta \\in \\Mor_\\mathcal{C}(w, y)$", "MATH_0010": "$\\gamma\\in \\Mor_{\\mathcal C}(w, x \\times y)$", "MATH_0011": "$$\n\\xymatrix{\nw \\ar[rrrd]^\\beta \\ar@{-->}[rrd]_\\gamma \\ar[rrdd]_\\alpha & & \\\\\n& & x \\times y \\ar[d]_p \\ar[r]_q & y \\\\\n& & x &\n}\n$$", "TEXTITCLOSE_0001": "}", "TEXTITOPEN_0001": "{\\it "}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{definition}\n\\label{definition-products}\n", "suffix": "\\end{definition}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:089d5345267bcdb4bea99bb302d625135621b9045063dfcd21e808d6be748620", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:19bed65c0125a7bc11a3d9ae050b3acfd2153c59aa55579f379c3e3837f3b6eb", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001>.\nA <TEXTITOPEN_0001>product<TEXTITCLOSE_0001> of <MATH_0002> and <MATH_0003> is\nan object <MATH_0004>\ntogether with morphisms\n<MATH_0005> and\n<MATH_0006> such\nthat the following universal property holds: for\nany <MATH_0007> and morphisms\n<MATH_0008> and\n<MATH_0009>\nthere is a unique\n<MATH_0010> making\nthe diagram\n<MATH_0011>\ncommute.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:eaa886596a9a635d9b55973f956a53d02d8c1619344cdc3bd582c0ee1f8661d5", "unit_id": "tag:001S:statement"}
{"chapter": "categories", "node_kind": "definition", "parent_tag": "001R", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0002": "$x \\times y$", "MATH_0003": "$x, y \\in \\Ob(\\mathcal{C})$", "TEXTITCLOSE_0001": "}", "TEXTITOPEN_0001": "{\\it "}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{definition}\n\\label{definition-has-products-of-pairs}\n", "suffix": "\\end{definition}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:f992f637101cbeb027b53af415744ed92756e34af06eff3436d8c56c785af255", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:6dcab11f5fa9e3511d3fa4f6f8c15d958780b0d6bddbf910d9dadc76c3d9953c", "source_text": "We say the category <MATH_0001> <TEXTITOPEN_0001>has products of pairs\nof objects<TEXTITCLOSE_0001> if a product <MATH_0002>\nexists for any <MATH_0003>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:a91dd10ebff37e8bfd25b3be53e344469636407354bfd900874a0e1ebdf41e44", "unit_id": "tag:001T:statement"}
{"chapter": "categories", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "001R", "placeholders": {"STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:85c6b45a3dd73fb6e90f01a45d7af284b6e81fa37a31b0cc1005e50168137844", "source_text": "<STRUCT_0001>\nWe use this terminology to distinguish this notion from the notion\nof ``having products'' or ``having finite products'' which usually means\nsomething else (in particular it always implies there exists a\nfinal object).", "source_text_hash": "sha256:5cc9dcb1f163ac64b91e0b17dbe0bd2d6a543f51e07be823b8161214f7342ede", "unit_id": "tag:001R:paragraph-0002"}
