{"chapter": "categories", "node_kind": "definition", "parent_tag": "001U", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$x, y, z\\in \\Ob(\\mathcal{C})$", "MATH_0002": "$f\\in \\Mor_\\mathcal{C}(x, y)$", "MATH_0003": "$g\\in \\Mor_{\\mathcal C}(z, y)$", "MATH_0004": "$f$", "MATH_0005": "$g$", "MATH_0006": "$x \\times_y z\\in \\Ob(\\mathcal{C})$", "MATH_0007": "$p \\in \\Mor_{\\mathcal C}(x \\times_y z, x)$", "MATH_0008": "$q \\in \\Mor_{\\mathcal C}(x \\times_y z, z)$", "MATH_0009": "$$\n\\xymatrix{\nx \\times_y z \\ar[r]_q \\ar[d]_p & z \\ar[d]^g \\\\\nx \\ar[r]^f & y\n}\n$$", "MATH_0010": "$w\\in \\Ob(\\mathcal{C})$", "MATH_0011": "$\\alpha \\in \\Mor_{\\mathcal C}(w, x)$", "MATH_0012": "$\\beta \\in \\Mor_\\mathcal{C}(w, z)$", "MATH_0013": "$f \\circ \\alpha = g \\circ \\beta$", "MATH_0014": "$\\gamma \\in \\Mor_{\\mathcal C}(w, x \\times_y z)$", "MATH_0015": "$$\n\\xymatrix{\nw \\ar[rrrd]^\\beta \\ar@{-->}[rrd]_\\gamma \\ar[rrdd]_\\alpha & & \\\\\n& & x \\times_y z \\ar[d]^p \\ar[r]_q & z \\ar[d]^g \\\\\n& & x \\ar[r]^f & y\n}\n$$", "TEXTITCLOSE_0001": "}", "TEXTITOPEN_0001": "{\\it "}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{definition}\n\\label{definition-fibre-products}\n", "suffix": "\\end{definition}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:2e1d980ba7906cf25052130f400441a7be38e9f98b4815e3786ba5feb98f6d1d", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:c89a7deaeb78e05a8a0c13faa2d9dacad728e573d03b0cd0ea933873ad68510c", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001>,\n<MATH_0002>\nand <MATH_0003>.\nA <TEXTITOPEN_0001>fibre product<TEXTITCLOSE_0001> of <MATH_0004> and <MATH_0005> is\nan object <MATH_0006>\ntogether with morphisms\n<MATH_0007> and\n<MATH_0008> making the diagram\n<MATH_0009>\ncommute, and such that the following universal property holds: for\nany <MATH_0010> and morphisms\n<MATH_0011> and\n<MATH_0012> with\n<MATH_0013>\nthere is a unique\n<MATH_0014> making\nthe diagram\n<MATH_0015>\ncommute.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:eda9ef8651cb3dc8319c39f5014bd6a08a241081d75cb0aacb582389587f4788", "unit_id": "tag:001V:statement"}
{"chapter": "categories", "node_kind": "definition", "parent_tag": "001U", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$f : x \\to y$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0003": "$z \\to y$", "MATH_0004": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0005": "$x \\times_y z$", "TEXTITCLOSE_0001": "}", "TEXTITOPEN_0001": "{\\it "}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{definition}\n\\label{definition-representable-morphism}\n", "suffix": "\\end{definition}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:15b6b20253f4eeccb0f1d296054f2e9cb5f1860a67a87ec84ef56a7eab05a6f5", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:6b52f84d3aa335ff85a53fd83a85c0ccce8438333084df7e7f4920a62396777a", "source_text": "A morphism <MATH_0001> of a category <MATH_0002> is said to be\n<TEXTITOPEN_0001>representable<TEXTITCLOSE_0001> if for every morphism <MATH_0003>\nin <MATH_0004> the fibre product <MATH_0005> exists.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:55608759830a7b4b8210043593a1f0bf794fc12c0a718d6f4bb9cf67d784464c", "unit_id": "tag:001X:statement"}
{"chapter": "categories", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "001U", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0002": "$f : x \\to y$", "MATH_0003": "$y' \\to y$", "MATH_0004": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0005": "$x' := x \\times_y y' \\to y'$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-base-change-representable}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:ce0ffe2f34290e446cb6a9cb99929242e23b1250b308e52cd2d76112adf80519", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:28cfb6a0cc98ce1b0a5605c96aa493bd9b13d2a6fb3592e6efcd9bc8497dffe4", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a category.\nLet <MATH_0002> be representable.\nLet <MATH_0003> be a morphism of <MATH_0004>.\nThen the morphism <MATH_0005> is representable also.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:81f9702baf39669628b757bcf60c9247df477f0b0be9cae97027f8037319760f", "unit_id": "tag:001Z:statement"}
{"chapter": "categories", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "001U", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$z \\to y'$", "MATH_0002": "$x' \\times_{y'} z$", "MATH_0003": "\\begin{eqnarray*}\nw & \\mapsto & h_{x'}(w)\\times_{h_{y'}(w)} h_z(w) \\\\\n& = & (h_x(w) \\times_{h_y(w)} h_{y'}(w)) \\times_{h_{y'}(w)} h_z(w) \\\\\n& = & h_x(w) \\times_{h_y(w)} h_z(w)\n\\end{eqnarray*}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:2107382a226002c68bfb1b8a439e28759961605a9d89bc96fe156236ce6cbb7c", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:9639072ea5f4ef4547cf96290975134ef10e2189bd7cd2f83890375e10b0341b", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a morphism. The fibre product\n<MATH_0002> is supposed to represent the\nfunctor\n<MATH_0003>\nwhich is representable by assumption.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:8ae973deb3f21d0213e717a4029777dfac513be771f169d63871222f2aa7101e", "unit_id": "tag:001Z:proof"}
